+### 1.1 Half-launched task after a tmux window failure
+
+`hive-launch` provisions the clones, wrapper, and board assignment before it creates
+the named tmux window. If window creation fails, its stderr says **“window creation
+failed after board seeding”** and prints a filled kickoff. This is a half-launched
+task: confirm the task is `assigned`, and confirm the worker clone and wrapper named
+in the message exist. The board assignment is durable even though no pane exists.
+
+Do **not** re-run `hive-launch`; it will refuse the already-assigned task and cannot
+repair this state. Use the exact `tmux new-window -a` command printed by the failure
+message (append/free-slot allocation, with the task name and filled `HIVE_KICKOFF`).
+If the session itself is absent, use the printed `tmux new-session` alternative.
+Then verify that the window is named for the task and that the worker starts from the
+filled kickoff. If it does not start, paste that kickoff into the worker command and
+have it emit `task.accepted` through the issued wrapper.
+
+Only use the normal dead-worker recovery path — `task.reassigned` as described in
+WORKER.md §Launch — when the worker is genuinely dead after the pane has been
+recovered. Reassignment is not a substitute for completing the missing pane.
+
